Two things make it correct: `mutate()` detaches the drawable from the shared constant state so greying out one icon can no longer leak into other instances, and the alpha is now driven off `isEnabled()` on *every* pass, so the enabled branches actively restore full opacity instead of inheriting stale state. Existing behaviour (icon choice, enablement rules, disabled appearance) is unchanged.

`./gradlew clean assembleDebug` → **BUILD SUCCESSFUL**.

