The edit is applied (the project sits inside a git-ignored `runs/` path, so `git diff` shows nothing — the patch is below).

## Diagnosis

`Reviewer.onCreateOptionsMenu()` chose the undo/eraser icon like this:

- whiteboard undo stack non-empty → eraser icon (left enabled, alpha untouched)
- whiteboard used but stack empty → eraser icon + `setEnabled(false).getIcon().setAlpha(ALPHA_ICON_DISABLED_LIGHT)`

The defect is in the disabled branch. `MenuItem.getIcon()` returns a drawable inflated from the resource cache; without `mutate()`, all instances of `R.drawable.ic_eraser_variant_white_24dp` share one `ConstantState`, and for a `VectorDrawable` the root alpha lives in that shared state. So once the eraser is greyed out, alpha 76 is baked into the cached state process-wide.

When the user redraws, `Whiteboard.drawFinish()` correctly calls `supportInvalidateOptionsMenu()` (stack size 0 → 1) and the menu is re-inflated into the enabled branch — but that branch never restores the alpha, so the freshly created drawable comes back out of the cache still at alpha 76. The button is clickable, yet permanently looks greyed out. Same latent issue for `ic_undo_white_24dp`.

## Fix

`AnkiDroid/src/main/java/com/ichi2/anki/Reviewer.java`

